  {
    "startIndex": 114848,
    "endIndex": 115177,
    "paragraph": {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 114848,
          "endIndex": 115177,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "The application provides Live, Practice, Glosses and History functions. Live captures signing and presents recognition feedback, accepted glosses and generated English. Practice supports interaction with the selected vocabulary, while Glosses provides access to the supported signs. History allows saved sessions to be reviewed.\n",
            "textStyle": {
              "fontSize": {
                "magnitude": 12,
                "unit": "PT"
              },
              "weightedFontFamily": {
                "fontFamily": "Times New Roman",
                "weight": 400
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphStyle": {
        "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
        "alignment": "JUSTIFIED",
        "lineSpacing": 200,
        "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
        "spaceAbove": {
          "unit": "PT"
        },
        "spaceBelow": {
          "unit": "PT"
        },
        "indentFirstLine": {
          "magnitude": 36,
          "unit": "PT"
        },
        "indentStart": {
          "unit": "PT"
        },
        "indentEnd": {
          "unit": "PT"
        },
        "keepLinesTogether": true,
        "keepWithNext": false
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "startIndex": 115177,
    "endIndex": 115578,
    "paragraph": {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 115177,
          "endIndex": 115578,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "During Live operation, camera frames supply landmark and hand-image inputs. The boundary detector and recognizer provide evidence for candidate intervals, and the segmental decoder accepts a gloss sequence. English generation operates on the accumulated glosses. The Finish control signals message completion, after which the application finalizes the remaining text and provides local speech output.\n",
            "textStyle": {
              "fontSize": {
                "magnitude": 12,
                "unit": "PT"
              },
              "weightedFontFamily": {
                "fontFamily": "Times New Roman",
                "weight": 400
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphStyle": {
        "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
        "alignment": "JUSTIFIED",
        "lineSpacing": 200,
        "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT",
        "spaceAbove": {
          "unit": "PT"
        },
        "spaceBelow": {
          "unit": "PT"
        },
        "indentFirstLine": {
          "magnitude": 36,
          "unit": "PT"
        },
        "indentStart": {
          "unit": "PT"
        },
        "indentEnd": {
          "unit": "PT"
        },
        "keepLinesTogether": true,
        "keepWithNext": false
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "startIndex": 115578,
    "endIndex": 115866,
    "paragraph": {
      "elements": [
        {
          "startIndex": 115578,
          "endIndex": 115866,
          "textRun": {
            "content": "The application presents predictions within the selected vocabulary. Recognition is limited to the selected vocabulary and remains sensitive to the quality and completeness of the captured input. User-facing feedback allows the recognized sequence to be inspected during the interaction.\n",
            "textStyle": {
              "fontSize": {
                "magnitude": 12,
                "unit": "PT"
              },
              "weightedFontFamily": {
                "fontFamily": "Times New Roman",
                "weight": 400
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphStyle": {
